from pathlib import Path
import json,html
out=Path('final-navigation-audit');records=[r for r in json.loads((out/'headers-before.json').read_text()) if 'audit' not in r['page']];(out/'changed-header-pages.json').write_text(json.dumps([r['page'] for r in records],indent=2))
source=json.loads((out/'source-verification.json').read_text());mapping=json.loads((out/'considerations-map.json').read_text())
rows=''.join('<tr><td>'+html.escape(label)+'</td><td>'+html.escape(m['newCategory'])+'</td><td><a href="../'+m['url']+'">'+m['url']+'</a></td><td>'+str(len(source['formerConsiderations'][label]['articles']))+'</td></tr>' for label,m in mapping.items())
cards=''
for w,title in [(1440,'Desktop'),(1024,'iPad landscape'),(768,'iPad portrait'),(390,'Phone')]:
 states=['closed','buy'] if w>=1024 else ['closed','menu','buy']
 cards+='<section><h2>'+title+' · '+str(w)+'px</h2><div class="gallery">'+''.join('<figure><a href="'+str(w)+'-'+state+'.png"><img loading="lazy" src="'+str(w)+'-'+state+'.png" alt="'+title+' '+state+' navigation"></a><figcaption>'+state.title()+'</figcaption></figure>' for state in states)+'</div></section>'
extra=' '.join('<a href="'+str(w)+'-closed.png">'+str(w)+'px</a>' for w in [1920,1440,1280,1024,820,768,600,390,320])
(out/'review.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>DommyDom navigation · local review</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f8f7f3;color:#343c32;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:32px}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400;color:#48533e}a{color:#48533e}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:white}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cdd1c3}section{margin:40px 0}.gallery{display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:start;flex-wrap:wrap}figure{margin:0;flex:1;min-width:260px;max-width:680px}img{display:block;width:100%;border:1px solid #cdd1c3}figcaption{padding:8px 0;font-size:14px}.notice{border-left:4px solid #48533e;padding:16px;background:white}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:16px}table{font-size:12px}td,th{padding:7px}}</style><main><h1>DommyDom navigation</h1><p class="notice">Local implementation for owner review. Nothing has been published, pushed, or deployed.</p><p><strong>Home · About · Buy · Sell · Property Management · Interior Design · Life Changes · Blog · Contact</strong></p><p>Search is a separate icon and visible label at the upper-right, linking to the existing search.html page. Desktop dropdowns open on hover and keyboard focus without arrows. On touch, tap a category to open its submenu; its overview link remains available. Narrow screens show the nine primary categories in one flow, with one submenu level and Back/Close controls.</p><p>Header markup and its stylesheet reference were updated consistently on all 351 live HTML pages. The shared files are <code>assets/navigation-v22.js</code> and <code>assets/responsive-navigation.css</code>. The existing menu scroll-lock helper is retained. Historical audit snapshots are unchanged. <a href="changed-header-pages.json">Complete page list</a>.</p><h2>Former Considerations destinations</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Destination</th><th>New menu</th><th>Unchanged URL</th><th>Articles</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table><p>All 45 articles retain their existing landing pages and URLs. Life Changes retains its overview and all seven topic links; the four former Search valley-guide links are retained under Buy → Cities. All 68 original distinct header destinations remain available. No original navigation URLs were broken. No page copy, dates, metadata, imagery, or approved section designs changed outside the header and its stylesheet reference.</p><p>Verification: six page types at nine widths (54 combinations), plus actual Search navigation, a relocated Buying link, primary category navigation, keyboard focus/Escape, touch submenus, focus containment, backdrop dismissal, background scrolling, and rotation/resizing. These are local Chrome previews with simulated touch; no physical iPad was used. Remote integrations were blocked during layout checks; no forms were submitted.</p><p><a href="browser-results.json">Layout results</a> · <a href="interaction-results.json">Interaction results</a> · <a href="source-verification.json">Content and URL audit</a></p>'''+cards+'<h2>All requested widths</h2><p>'+extra+'</p></main></html>',encoding='utf-8')
